const obj = { seq, at, kind, recordId, data, prevHash };
canonical = JSON.stringify(obj, Object.keys(obj).sort());

Our computeHash uses entryWithoutHash which includes same fields. Should match. Why not? Let's extract actual second entry from failing test to see values. We'll write a script to create ledger with two entries and log second entry and expected hash.

